  "reconstruction": {
    "scope": "Specific standing Mars Ultor temple remains: occupied raised podium and wide frontal stair with central rough altar remnant; four mapped broken front shafts, three tall mapped fluted Corinthian columns/short surviving entablature and rear pilaster; low fragmentary cella/apse masonry. Include mapped high rear firewall and lower right return with true round-arched Pantani passage. No restored complete roof, pediment, full colonnade, cult statues or copied sculpture/photo atlas. Independent neighboring houses and other Forum ruins remain native.",
    "identityBasis": "Standard PMTiles named Temple of Mars Ultor POI52776571486298 and archaeological POI17604119328229 correlate candidateQ679665. Thirteen actual ruin/column/entablature/firewall controls fix their positions; no exact-QID building footprint claim. Front mapped corner stumps35184512353546/35184574043290 fix cross-axis and approximately31m front width; tall southeast side column controls35184574043288/35185367502449/35185367502448 and pilaster35185367502447 fix the surviving group. Anchor12.486844,41.894283; heading0/native east-south axes; local origin at front-row midpoint and cross-axis about+.855rad. Front stair faces southwest/local+z. Podium/cella envelope is an explicit picture-led approximation fitted around these controls, not a mapped roof footprint.",
    "heightBasis": "Picture/map estimates: occupied podium34.4m wide and about40m deep, local floor3.4m above anchor datum and broad18-step approach. Three white Corinthian columns15.2m above floor plus roughly1.2m entablature; four broken front shafts retain distinct heights4.6/2.6/2.9/2.4m. High firewall top29m above datum, lower right return15.5m; approximate Pantani opening4.6m wide,5m spring and7.3m crown. Hidden cella/apse allocation, wall ruin inventory, masonry holes/repairs and absolute archaeological levels remain approximate.",
    "terrainBasis": "Reuse the existing pinned standard Rome Protomaps/Mapzen extract and retain original6m terrain, native paths/water and all independent building inputs. Level occupied temple podium and narrow wall footings have buried bases; short graded stair approach. No broad Forum/plaza slab, terrain flattening or native ground/water cutout. Coarse DEM cannot resolve excavated paving, upper street levels, grass-covered cella or exact thresholds; occupied podium top uses shared pale stone and soft noise-tinted vegetation patches rather than claiming literal surviving paving/plant inventory.",
